## Solution
The cross product of vectors $\mathbf{u} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 2 \\ -6 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ is given by the formula
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{u} \times \mathbf{v} = \begin{vmatrix} \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\ 5 & 2 & -6 \\ 1 & 1 & 3 \end{vmatrix}.
\end{equation}
Expanding the determinant, we have
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{u} \times \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 2\cdot3 - (-6)\cdot1 \\ -6\cdot1 - 5\cdot3 \\ 5\cdot1 - 2\cdot1 \end{pmatrix} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 12 \\ -21 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}}.
\end{equation}
Therefore, the answer to the problem is $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 12 \\ -21 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}}$.

